# The generated SECRET_KEY. .gitignore calls this out by name as a live
# credential -- it lands in the repo root after any local alembic/seed/uvicorn
# run -- and `COPY . .` was baking it into a shared image layer, recoverable by
# anyone with `docker save` or registry pull access. The container never READS
# it (on Postgres there is nowhere to persist one), so this is disclosure into a
# distributable artifact rather than a runtime weakening -- but it is exactly
# the failure .gitignore was written to prevent, missed one file over.
.printer-nanny-secret-key
# Its own example shows an operator putting a Postgres URL with a password here.
docker-compose.override.yml
